From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usermode-helper: crash_reporter by its merged-/usr path too

NickelOS Unified's root is merged /usr: /sbin leads to /usr/bin.
crash_reporter writes its own path, as it resolves, into the kernel's
core_pattern (/usr/bin/crash_reporter), and usermode-helper refused it,
so no crash was ever collected. Accept that path as Google already does
for modprobe.

---
--- a/init/usermode-helper_lib.cc
+++ b/init/usermode-helper_lib.cc
@@ -164,7 +164,10 @@
 bool ValidateProgramArgs(int argc, const char* argv[]) {
   const std::string_view prog(argv[0]);
 
-  if (prog == "/sbin/crash_reporter") {
+  // NickelOS Unified: /sbin leads to /usr/bin (merged /usr), and crash_reporter
+  // writes its own path, as it resolves, into the kernel's core_pattern.
+  if ((prog == "/sbin/crash_reporter") ||
+      (prog == "/usr/bin/crash_reporter")) {
     return ValidateCrashReporter(argc, argv);
   } else if ((prog == "/usr/bin/modprobe") || (prog == "/sbin/modprobe")) {
     return ValidateModprobe(argc, argv);
